      {
        "label": "D-1 Cut over the pilot with Postgres logical replication",
        "raw": "/projects/2415ccf7-9c11-4023-b933-f5ab9db037d3/decisions?decision=ed772b25-a0de-45e6-b207-108169f39486",
        "href": "/projects/2415ccf7-9c11-4023-b933-f5ab9db037d3/decisions?decision=ed772b25-a0de-45e6-b207-108169f39486",
        "targetId": "ed772b25-a0de-45e6-b207-108169f39486",
        "resolves": true
      }
    ],
    "answer": "Postgres logical replication was chosen for the pilot cut-over as a simpler alternative to an application-layer dual-write. The application-layer approach was rejected because it would touch nineteen write paths in the payments service and require four to five weeks of work, whereas the rollback benefit it provides is not needed at pilot volume. [D-1 Cut over the pilot with Postgres logical replication](/projects/2415ccf7-9c11-4023-b933-f5ab9db037d3/decisions?decision=ed772b25-a0de-45e6-b207-108169f39486)",
    "finishReason": "stop"
  },
