      },
      {
        "label": "D-5 Extend the pilot to fourteen merchants",
        "raw": "/projects/2415ccf7-9c11-4023-b933-f5ab9db037d3/decisions?decision=1a34c512-9fdc-497c-a07c-9b75f49edcc3",
        "href": "/projects/2415ccf7-9c11-4023-b933-f5ab9db037d3/decisions?decision=1a34c512-9fdc-497c-a07c-9b75f49edcc3",
        "targetId": "1a34c512-9fdc-497c-a07c-9b75f49edcc3",
        "resolves": true
      }
    ],
    "answer": "The eleven-merchant pilot size was chosen because the vendor reconciliation service cannot take a larger volume yet. [Steering committee minutes - September](/projects/2415ccf7-9c11-4023-b933-f5ab9db037d3/evidence?item=e8a21860-86e9-4216-8d1f-7a331a9e94bb#evidence-e8a21860-86e9-4216-8d1f-7a331a9e94bb) The original plan called for a twenty-five merchant pilot, but that was rejected due to the vendor's capacity constraints. [D-2 Limit the pilot to eleven merchants](/projects/2415ccf7-9c11-4023-b933-f5ab9db037d3/decisions?decision=25b25d39-ae87-4190-9c0c-17dcc05ca2ab)\n\nHowever, this decision has since been superseded. The pilot has now been extended to fourteen merchants, since three additional merchants asked to join and the reconciliation harness now covers their settlement plan. [D-5 Extend the pilot to fourteen merchants](/projects/2415ccf7-9c11-4023-b933-f5ab9db037d3/decisions?decision=1a34c512-9fdc-497c-a07c-9b75f49edcc3)",
    "finishReason": "stop"
  },
