    "answer": "The argument against application-layer dual-write was threefold: it would touch nineteen write paths in the payments service, require four to five weeks of work, and the rollback benefit is not needed at pilot volume. [Architecture review call](/projects/2415ccf7-9c11-4023-b933-f5ab9db037d3/evidence?item=7a71e3e3-21a1-443b-afd3-5a74b1773d02#evidence-7a71e3e3-21a1-443b-afd3-5a74b1773d02)\n\nThis rejection led to the decision to use Postgres logical replication for the pilot cut-over instead. [D-1 Cut over the pilot with Postgres logical replication](/projects/2415ccf7-9c11-4023-b933-f5ab9db037d3/decisions?decision=ed772b25-a0de-45e6-b207-108169f39486)",
    "finishReason": "stop"
  },
